cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - name: RakTikoo
title: "blockrandom: seeded permuted-block randomization lists for small clinical trials"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-17
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/RakTikoo/blockrandom"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RakTikoo/blockrandom"
abstract: >-
  Generates seeded permuted-block randomization lists for small
  clinical trials — stratified, reproducible byte-for-byte from a
  recorded seed, with a full allocation list, a sealed enrolment
  list, per-stratum files, an audit log and a ready-to-paste methods
  paragraph. A seed is required; the tool refuses to invent one.
  Research and educational tool only; not a medical device. It gives
  no diagnosis, staging, or dose or treatment advice.
keywords:
  - randomization
  - permuted blocks
  - clinical trials
  - reproducibility
  - stratification
